Description: Enable 3D off starts flat; the told-once notice after the view has drawn
 Patch 0001 makes Crystal Eyes ParaView's configured stereo type, so with Enable 3D
 off the render view gets the native (mono) widget while the type is still Crystal
 Eyes, and pqQVTKWidget asked the stereo widget, which was not made, for its stereo
 format: a null pointer and a crash at every start (Qt/Core/pqQVTKWidget.cxx, the
 request after "if active stereo requested"). The request is now made only when the
 stereo-capable widget was made.
 .
 The notice that a saved setting or state file asked for one of ParaView's former
 output formats was opened while ParaView was still starting; Qt then replaces the
 main window's platform window when the view's OpenGL window is put in it, and the
 notice was closed with the old one before it was ever on screen (measured: opened
 2.4 s before the main window's first show, closed 0.7 s after its second). It now
 opens after the view's next frame (pqView::endRender), once the main window is
 exposed, and its sentence also goes to the log at INFO.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-21

--- a/Qt/Core/pqQVTKWidget.cxx
+++ b/Qt/Core/pqQVTKWidget.cxx
@@ -85,7 +85,9 @@
 
   // if active stereo requested, then we need to request appropriate context.
   auto config = vtkRemotingCoreConfiguration::GetInstance();
-  if (config->GetStereoType() == VTK_STEREO_CRYSTAL_EYES)
+  // Sparky Stereo OS: Crystal Eyes is the configured type also with Enable 3D off, when the view
+  // gets the native (mono) widget: only the stereo-capable widget takes the stereo format.
+  if (this->useStereo && config->GetStereoType() == VTK_STEREO_CRYSTAL_EYES)
   {
 #if PARAVIEW_USING_QVTKOPENGLSTEREOWIDGET
     auto fmt = baseClass.value<pqQVTKWidgetBase*>()->defaultFormat(/*supports_stereo =*/true);
